# Downloaded source catalogues. Reproducible: `python data/sources.py` fetches them again,
# and every file records where it came from. They are large and not ours to redistribute.
data/raw/

# The built catalogue, in both forms. Reproducible from data/raw by
# `py -3.12 data/build_catalogue.py`, which is the command the app's failure screen prints.
# Committing them would mean reviewing a 450 KB generated diff on every catalogue change, and
# would let the asset drift away from the sources it came from.
app/assets/starmap.db
app/assets/stars.json

# NOT ignored, on purpose: app/test/fixtures/horizons.json. Those are NASA's reference positions
# and the tests must run without a network. Committing them also means a change in the reference
# shows up as a reviewable diff instead of silently moving the goalposts.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Flutter / Dart
app/.dart_tool/
app/.flutter-plugins
app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
app/build/
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/local.properties
app/ios/Pods/
app/ios/.symlinks/
app/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
app/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
app/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
*.iml

